The dashed curve is $y=x^{2}$ and the solid curve is a dilation of it; the point $(1,1)$ maps to $(1,3)$. Which equation matches the solid curve?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.7)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-1.78:1.78,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.05:1.05,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*\x*\x});
\node[gray,right] at (1.4,2.4) {$y=x^{2}$};
\fill[gray] (1,1) circle (1.5pt) node[below right] {$(1,1)$};
\fill (1,3) circle (2pt) node[above] {$(1,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
